# The opening cutscene of a new voyage: the night the lantern pulled you
# from the sea. Played by the Opening node in scenes/prototype/sea.tscn.
# Placeholder writing: rewrite freely.
#
# A cutscene is a conversation whose @ cues stage the scene. Lines wait for
# the Interact button; cues that take time (a fade, a wait) hold the script
# until they're done. Every cue is listed in scripts/cutscene/cue_list.gd.
#
# Shots (where the camera goes) and marks (where people stand) are Marker3D
# nodes in scenes/prototype/ship.tscn, under Shots and Marks: drag them in
# the editor to reframe a shot, without touching this file.
#
# To tune one beat: set Start Section on the Opening node to its name
# (waking, doorway, stove) and the game opens there. While it runs, F8
# reads this file again and replays the section you're in.

# Black, and where we are. The captain isn't in the room yet.
~ start
@hide heron
@title Somewhere at sea
@wait 2.5
@fade in 2.0
-> waking

# You wake by your bunk, the lantern across the room.
~ waking
lantern: There you are.
lantern: You were in the water. I pulled. You held on. Good holding.
lantern: I'll get you home. I know exactly where it is. Roughly.
@wait 0.6
-> doorway

# A tall shadow in the doorway: the captain, come to look you over.
~ doorway
@place heron doorway
@show heron
@face heron player
@shot doorway cut
@wait 0.8
heron: Nobody drowns on my ship. Nobody goes hungry either.
heron: You've managed the first.
-> stove

# Through to the galley: something has been left warm on the stove. While
# we look at it, the captain goes back to the fire. Then the ship is yours.
~ stove
@shot pot_on_stove
@home heron
@wait 2.5
@shot free cut
